      "source": "2026-06-17 Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool post-restoration Washington DC 18-53-22",
      "description": "The Washington Monument reflecting in the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool after the pool was restored and painted blue.  There is currently an algae bloom being cleaned up and equipment related to that cleanup is visible on the right side of the pool. At this point the algae has been cleared from the water and has settled on the bottom of the pool. In some places it has been vacuumed up but in other places the bottom of the pool is green.  Since the Washington Monument and the sky is being reflected, the color of the water and base of the pool isn't clearly visible. There are also temporary lights lining both sides of the reflecting pool. National Mall, Washington, DC. June 17, 2026.",
